<title>USA: U.S. power output falls 2.5 pct vs. year ago - EEI.</title>
<headline>U.S. power output falls 2.5 pct vs. year ago - EEI.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electricity deliveries in the continental U.S. totaled 63,264 gigawatt hours (GWh) for the week ended Dec 14, down 2.5 percent from the same period in 1995, the Edison Electric Institute (EEI) said.</p>
<p>The amount of weekly power supplied to the Mid-Atlantic area slipped the most from a year ago, down 8.5 percent to 8,521 GWh, EEI said.</p>
<p>Year-to-date domestic power production totaled about 3.18 million GWh, up 2.3 percent from the same period in 1995, EEI said.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
